          "type": "turn",
          "question": "My husband's face is drooping on one side and he can't speak properly. Is this a stroke?",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services now.** Sudden drooping on one side of the face together with trouble speaking are recognised warning signs of a stroke. Treatment works best when it starts quickly. Do not drive him yourself, and do not wait to see if it passes. Note the time his symptoms started, or the last time he was known to be well, and tell the emergency team.\n\nI can't tell you whether this is a stroke. Only emergency staff can assess that, and they will check quickly. Your husband's symptoms match the pattern the guidance describes as needing emergency care, so that is the right step now.\n\nThe guidance I found says a sudden change in the face, arm, or speech, along with sudden confusion, vision changes, trouble walking, or a sudden severe headache, all need emergency assessment. My search for other conditions did not return a clear match for this combination, so I won't suggest any alternative explanation. Please don't wait for a clinician to confirm it before calling for help.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
